STILL OPEN
================================================================================

- A wk user service that starts and then dies is reported as started. The
  vmtools stage asks `systemctl --user is-active --quiet` straight after
  `enable --now`, and a service that execs and fails a fraction of a second
  later answers active at that instant (measured: wk-github-inject with no
  PrivateTmp restarted 36 times while ./setup called it started). The three
  services do this three times, so the fix is one helper beside
  `unit_install` (host/units.sh) that asks systemd for readiness rather than
  for liveness at t=0 -- `Type=notify` and a sd_notify in the two Python
  services is the off-the-shelf answer; a settle-and-look-again is not.

- Two podman bugs to upstream, both worked around here and both silent:
  `podman machine init --volume src:target:ro` generates a systemd .mount
  unit with no `ro` in Options (podman 5.4, applehv), so the guest mounts it
  read-write and a write reaches the host; and it names the unit after the
  target it was handed without canonicalising it against the machine OS, so a
  target under a symlinked directory produces a unit systemd refuses to mount
  and a machine that comes up without it.

- The `remote` target has no ssh-agent, so `wk push` on a build box reports
  "always live, no switch on this machine" (remote/provision.sh points
  core.sshCommand at the private half). Installing wk-ssh-agent.service there
  through host/units.sh is the owed work (docs/HANDOFF-sandboxing.md).

